{
  "source": "RSA toy example: Wikipedia 'RSA (cryptosystem)' and many textbooks use p=61, q=53, e=17, d=2753, n=3233, with m=65 encrypting to c=2790. Modular exponent example 4^13 mod 497 = 445 is a common RSA tutorial check.",
  "vectors": [
